romanized_response:
HTTP status code 429 Too Many Requests andre server ge ondu thara rate limit ide mattu nimma request adanna meeride antha artha. Idu ee kelagina yavudaadru karanadinda agirabahudu:

1. Ee request maaduva code anna kadime samayadalli tumba sala run maadiddiri, adarinda rate limit cross aagide.

2. Website tanage spam antha anumana barva requests galanna 429 status code jote reject maadutte. Idarartha user agent ondu common browser alla antha, idu kelavu websites use maaduva ondu simple check. Idanna sariputtuvudakke, neevu GET request ge "User-Agent" header anna ee reeti add maadabahudu:

```
const response = await axios.get('https://www.realestate.com.au/rent/in-sydney,+nsw/list-1', 
     { headers: { 'User-Agent': 'browser.version' }  }
);
```

Gamanisi, neevu `"browser.version"` anna nijavada browser user agent string jote badalisabeku. Ee code yava application nalli run aaguttide annodara mele depend aagi, idu user agent spoofing antha pariganisabahudu, idu kelavu deshagalu athava organizations galu kanoonugala kelage (athava code access maadalu prayatnisuva website na terms of service kelage) nirbandhitavagirabahudu.

3. Website bere yavudo karanadinda requests galanna rate limit maaduttide. Idu request ondu proxy mulaka maadiddarinda agirabahudu, aa case nalli aa proxy na bere users tumba requests maadiruvudarinda agirabahudu, aadre idu sambhava kadime.

4. Website ella requests galanna reject maaduttide karana adu denial of service attack ge olagaagide. Idu sambhava kadime, yake andre such attack kelage server na typical behavior andre traffic anna ondu non-existent server ge route maaduvudu, athava completely deny maaduvudu, yavude valid response kodade. Aadre, website HTTP status code jote respond maadidaru, adu server error 503 Service Unavailable aagirava sadhyate jaasti, idu server overload aadaga sigutte.

response_en:
Yes, certainly! The issue you're encountering is because the string literals "fizzbuzz", "fizz", and "buzz" are temporary values, and you are trying to return a reference to them, which is not allowed because they will be dropped at the end of the scope, and the returned reference would be dangling.

You can fix this error by returning &'static str instead of &str. &'static str refers to string literals, which have a 'static lifetime, meaning they last for the duration of the program. Here's an updated version of your code:

fn fizzbuzz(n: usize) -> &'static str {
    match (n % 3, n % 5) {
        (0, 0) => "fizzbuzz",
        (0, _) => "fizz",
        (_, 0) => "buzz",
        _ => {
            let s = n.to_string();
            Box::leak(s.into_boxed_str())
        }
    }
}

Note that the last arm returns a &'static str that is created from a String using the Box::leak function, which takes ownership of a Box<T> and returns a pointer to its contents, effectively leaking it. This is safe because the returned pointer will last for the duration of the program, but it should be used with care as it will not be cleaned up automatically.

romanized_response:
Houdu, khanditavaagi! Neevu edurisuttiruva samasye eneandare, "fizzbuzz", "fizz", mattu "buzz" anno string literals temporary values aagive, mattu neevu avugala reference return maadalu try maaduttiddeera, idu allowed alla yaakandare avu scope na konegondu drop aagutte, mattu return aada reference dangling aagi biduttade.

Neevu &str badalu &'static str return maadidre ee error fix maadabahudu. &'static str string literals ge refer aaguttade, ivugalige 'static lifetime ide, andre ivu program duration vargu irutte. Illi nimma code na updated version ide:

fn fizzbuzz(n: usize) -> &'static str {
    match (n % 3, n % 5) {
        (0, 0) => "fizzbuzz",
        (0, _) => "fizz",
        (_, 0) => "buzz",
        _ => {
            let s = n.to_string();
            Box::leak(s.into_boxed_str())
        }
    }
}

Gamanisi, kone arm Box::leak function balasi String inda create maadida &'static str return maaduttade, idu Box<T> na ownership tagedukondu adara contents ge pointer return maaduttade, effectively adanna leak maaduttade. Idu safe yaakandare return aada pointer program duration vargu iruttade, aadre idanna jaagrutheinda balasabeku yaakandare idu automatically clean up aagolla.

response_en:
Merge sort is a divide and conquer algorithm that works by recursively splitting the input array in half until the arrays are split into single elements. Then, the sorted arrays are merged back together in sorted order.

The key benefits of merge sort over a simpler algorithm like bubble sort are:

1. It is a stable sort that does not change the relative order of elements with equal keys.
2. It has an efficiency of O(n log n) time complexity, making it a relatively efficient algorithm even for large input sizes. Bubble sort, on the other hand, has a quadratic time complexity of O(n^2), making it very inefficient for larger inputs.
3. It is a generic algorithm that can sort any type of data for which a comparison function exists.

Here is a Rust implementation example:
```rust
fn merge_sort(vec: &mut [i32]) {
    if vec.len() < 2 {
        return;
    }

    let mid = vec.len() / 2;
    let (left, right) = vec.split_at_mut(mid);

    merge_sort(left);
    merge_sort(right);

    merge(left, right, vec);
}

fn merge(left: &mut [i32], right: &mut [i32], vec: &mut [i32]) {
    let mut i = 0;
    let mut j = 0;
    let mut k = 0;

    while i < left.len() && j < right.len() {
        if left[i] < right[j] {
            vec[k] = left[i];
            i += 1;
        } else {
            vec[k] = right[j];
            j += 1;
        }
        k += 1;
    }

    while i < left.len() {
        vec[k] = left[i];
        i += 1;
        k += 1;
    }

    while j < right.len() {
        vec[k] = right[j];
        j += 1;
        k += 1;
    }
}
```

romanized_response:
Merge sort annodu ondu divide and conquer algorithm, idu input array annu recursively ardha ardha agi split madutte, kone ge arrays ondondu single element ge split agovavarege. Aamele, sorted arrays annu sorted order nalli vapas merge madlaagutte.

Bubble sort thara simple algorithm ge holisidre merge sort na mukhya benefits ivu:

1. Idu ondu stable sort, andre same keys irodu elements na relative order badalisalla.
2. Idara time complexity O(n log n), adrinda doddha input sizes ge kuda idu relatively efficient algorithm aagutte. Bubble sort ge bandre, adara time complexity quadratic O(n^2), adrinda doddha inputs ge tumba inefficient.
3. Idu generic algorithm, yaava type of data ge comparison function iddre adannu sort madbahudu.

Ige ondu Rust implementation example:
```rust
